sec.p:
The ETKA assay was selected for the laboratory assessment of thiamin status. ETKA was measured at baseline and after the addition of exogenous thiamin pyrophosphate using the method specified in a study by Densupsoontorn et al. [16]. The result, referred to as the thiamin pyrophosphate effect (TPPE), was calculated via the following formula:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\%TPPE=\left(\left[ETKA\, activated-ETKA\, basal\right]/ETKA\, basal\right)\times 100$$\end{document}%TPPE=ETKAactivated-ETKAbasal/ETKAbasal×100
